{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/605375-how-do-you-temper-stygian-steel-with-oblivion","id":605375,"title":"How do you \"temper\" Stygian Steel with Oblivion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-28T00:58:00-07:00","id":605375,"title":"How do you \"temper\" Stygian Steel with Oblivion?","content":"What does it mean to temper Stygian Steel with Oblivions? Do they mean Raw Angst collected by Castigators? Is there an Arcanos that we don't know about? Do they go beneath the labyrinth to dip the finished product in Oblivion? The phrase seems both odd and illogical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T05:37:20-07:00","id":605505,"title":"","content":"There is a great spiral stair that leads from the bottom of Stygia to the labyrinth. Chain gangs of drones scrape black stone off of the walls of that stair, and the scrapings are alloyed with the soulsteel of forged souls. The result is Stygian Steel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T14:02:09-07:00","id":605920,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but doesn't the tempering I part of forging something usually imply dipping it into something? It's been a while, but i thought smithies dipped their finished product into water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T19:49:05-07:00","id":606275,"title":"","content":"&quot;Tempering&quot; in blacksmithing refers to the heating/reheating and cooling of metals to increase their spring and hardiness. Most metals, like steel, are tempered by submerging them in oil, but some softer ones use water (usually when there's not danger from giant, scalding clouds of steam), and some are only sprayed - again, depending on what material one is working. Tempering is also used to create alloys, blends of two or more metals.<br /> <br /> In <i>Wraith</i>, the tempering of Stygian steel is properly an alloy, as it is the combination of soulsteel and death ore.<br /> <br /> This is, of course, a play on words, as to &quot;temper&quot; a thing is to make it less extreme, as well as make it more resilient.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T05:12:51-07:00","id":607668,"title":"","content":"And the author also could have made a mistake, not everyone who writes of smithing gets the steps right. I remember that Legend of Mana treated Tempering as the step to add exotic ingredients, like berries and wood. Strange game, that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}